host Ubuntu 26.04 LTS GNOME Wayland (cloud pier) — Eastern (EDT) time convention
title ALES87 — Lotus's center clipper, the static-curve sibling of the noise gate
prompt recur baton prin — take the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux-first lap, approve my own design round, send the finished increment to origin and xykj61, stop at custody gates
think The rectifier family closed at ALES86. Reading the DRIVE family for the next crux-first move: ALES78's hard clip caps the LOUD extremes at a ceiling but nothing yet silences the QUIET middle. The plain mirror is the center clipper — y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x — a dead zone carved out of the middle. Lindy (the classic hiss/crosstalk remover of Dolby/dbx and the exact model of crossover distortion in a class-B amp); crux-first (the DRIVE family's opener names its static-curve complement, and it keeps the recent memoryless-and-exact aesthetic the rectifiers set).
think Weighed a DC blocker (y = x − x₁ + R·y₁) as the alternative crux — highly Lindy, the companion the rectifier family's DC offset invites — yet its fractional feedback is a meatier, riskier round in integer PCM and the house already has a carried one-pole high-pass (ALES45). The center clipper is genuinely new, exact, memoryless, and self-contained: the cleaner crux for one signed round. Booked the DC blocker as a later self-approved round.
think The distinction from the noise gate (ALES51) is the teaching: the gate silences the whole wave when its LEVEL falls below a threshold — a dynamic decision with memory that opens and closes over time; the center clipper makes that same silencing STATIC and PER-SAMPLE, a fixed memoryless nonlinearity. The gate is a dynamics processor; the center clipper is a distortion curve. Exact for every i16 with no rail edge and no saturate — the only values written are 0 and the untouched input. The magnitude is taken in i32 so |sample_min| = 32768 is representable (the care the full-wave rectifier owed).
obs Followed the parametric-waveshaper pattern exactly (drive.rye): module + design doc + witness + README status-line sync and re-stamp + session log, one signed commit. Eight laws proven; the bracket reading pairs it with ALES78 (one caps the loud, one hollows the quiet). Postcondition split into two single asserts (out == 0 or out == dry; and the inclusive-boundary map). Witness GREEN on the first run; tame_style_check bans clean; width exit 0.
loom witness=ales_center_clip_witness selftest=GREEN laws=8 module_lines=173
file lotus/center_clip.rye the center clipper, y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x, exact for every i16 with no rail edge, eight laws proven
file tools/ales_center_clip_witness.rish builds the module, runs the selftest, asserts the single GREEN ales-center-clip line
file active-designing/20260814-215834_fill-ales87-lotus-center-clipper.md the self-approved design read naming the crux, the bracket, and the eight laws
file lotus/README.md front-door status line synced with ALES87 and re-stamped
recommend keep-going the DRIVE family now brackets the wave from both sides (the hard clip caps the loud, the center clip hollows the quiet); the loop names its own next Lotus crux — a soft dead-zone that subtracts the threshold rather than silencing to zero, or the booked DC blocker, or a fresh DSP family — as its own self-approved design round
